WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.834
-Hanging out with
Camila Cabello, everybody.

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:07.267
Oh, my gosh, "Familia"
is out right now.

00:00:07.267 --> 00:00:08.467
We're very excited.

00:00:08.467 --> 00:00:10.033
-We actually messed up
on something, though.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.334
-Oh? How?
-We totally should have gotten,

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:15.234
like, two tequila shots,
and just, like...

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:16.567
-And just went for it?
-Cheers.

00:00:16.567 --> 00:00:18.334
Yes. My album is out.

00:00:18.334 --> 00:00:19.534
Like what?

00:00:19.534 --> 00:00:21.534
It's okay.
We'll do it backstage.

00:00:21.534 --> 00:00:23.534
-No, no, no. Trust me,
this is the "Tonight Show."

00:00:23.534 --> 00:00:25.501
There is booze in every corner
of this place.

00:00:25.501 --> 00:00:27.334
-Just give us a damn shot.

00:00:27.334 --> 00:00:28.534
-[ Laughs ] Come on,
let's do it.

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:29.901
-I deserve a shot.
-Yeah, you deserve a shot.

00:00:29.901 --> 00:00:32.934
-You deserve a shot.
We all deserve shots!

00:00:32.934 --> 00:00:35.033
[ Cheering ]

00:00:35.033 --> 00:00:37.434
-They gotta drive home.
-No, yeah.

00:00:37.434 --> 00:00:39.901
We'll figure something out.

00:00:39.901 --> 00:00:42.567
We're talking about celebrating
moments

00:00:42.567 --> 00:00:44.467
and how we do have to
appreciate moments.

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:45.868
-Yeah.
-I do like that you said that.

00:00:45.868 --> 00:00:47.601
Because there are certain times
you kind of want to

00:00:47.601 --> 00:00:50.300
shake yourself and be like,
"Hey, this is crazy

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:51.734
what's happening right now.
Enjoy this."

00:00:51.734 --> 00:00:53.801
-This is significant.
-Yeah.

00:00:53.801 --> 00:00:56.467
"Havana," which you performed
at our show,

00:00:56.467 --> 00:00:58.534
which was one of our favorite
performances ever.

00:00:58.534 --> 00:01:01.067
-I mean, by the way, that
performance literally changed

00:01:01.067 --> 00:01:02.501
my career.

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:06.067
Like, I feel like the song blew
up after that performance.

00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.701
-It was insane in the way it
looked, and the red.

00:01:08.701 --> 00:01:10.234
It was just awesome and cool.

00:01:10.234 --> 00:01:13.067
I just saw you certified
diamond.

00:01:13.067 --> 00:01:14.400
-Yeah, what even is that?

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:15.934
[ Cheering ]

00:01:15.934 --> 00:01:19.234
-What? Like, where?
Do you, like...?

00:01:19.234 --> 00:01:22.067
-Like, I don't feel like my
brain can even compute

00:01:22.067 --> 00:01:24.033
what that number is.

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:26.133
-That's -- No one --
This doesn't happen.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:27.767
-Humans can't. We can't compute.

00:01:27.767 --> 00:01:29.300
-That's wild.
-That's a lot of people.

00:01:29.300 --> 00:01:32.200
-Also, you're so young.
You just started your career.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.167
And you're, like --
this is, like, awesome stuff.

00:01:34.167 --> 00:01:35.167
-It's only downhill from here.

00:01:35.167 --> 00:01:36.634
-[ Laughs ] No, no.

00:01:36.634 --> 00:01:38.067
No, it's nothing but better.

00:01:38.067 --> 00:01:40.267
Oh, my gosh,
it's all great stuff.

00:01:40.267 --> 00:01:41.701
-No, you know what? Listen.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:43.067
-It's all uphill from here? I
guess you can't say that either.

00:01:43.067 --> 00:01:45.667
-No, it is. No, it is.
Because here is the truth.

00:01:45.667 --> 00:01:47.968
I don't know when, whatever,
another diamond thing --

00:01:47.968 --> 00:01:49.868
it's very rare.
It's like lightning in a bottle.

00:01:49.868 --> 00:01:53.801
I don't know when or if that's
going to happen to me again.

00:01:53.801 --> 00:01:57.234
But I know it's uphill because
from that first album

00:01:57.234 --> 00:02:00.601
to this album,
I am, like, so much happier.

00:02:00.601 --> 00:02:05.868
I feel so much more, like,
creatively, like, happy.

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:09.434
And that's why, honestly, this
is -- this is my favorite album

00:02:09.434 --> 00:02:11.400
that I've ever done, like, from
a songwriter,

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:12.934
songwriting perspective.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:14.234
Like, I do feel
like it's uphill.

00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:16.434
Maybe there won't be another
diamond,

00:02:16.434 --> 00:02:18.434
but it's like I'm very --
emotionally --

00:02:18.434 --> 00:02:21.801
-I think you're going have
a bunch of diamonds.

00:02:21.801 --> 00:02:24.968
There's going to be just tons of
diamonds on this one.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.601
You're doing
"Saturday Night Live" tomorrow.

00:02:27.601 --> 00:02:30.067
I've seen you perform live
I don't know how many times.

00:02:30.067 --> 00:02:32.801
Do you get nervous
that it's live,

00:02:32.801 --> 00:02:35.300
or do you go, "No, this is --
I know how to perform."

00:02:35.300 --> 00:02:36.367
Let me show you.

00:02:36.367 --> 00:02:37.667
-I actually --
I love performing.

00:02:37.667 --> 00:02:40.300
I find that one
"Saturday Night Live," like --

00:02:40.300 --> 00:02:42.100
by the time I perform tomorrow,
that's usually, like,

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.834
when I'm in bed.
Like, that's usually, like,

00:02:43.834 --> 00:02:45.334
when I'm asleep.
It's like midnight.

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:46.634
-Yeah.
-When I start,

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:49.033
and so having that amount of
nerves and excitement

00:02:49.033 --> 00:02:52.100
and also being, like, sleepy

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:54.000
is, like,
a very confusing thing.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.968
It's like having coffee and wine
at the same time.

00:02:56.968 --> 00:02:58.534
-No, you won't be --
-It's like that.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:01.100
-You'll be so amped up.
-No -- Well, I know.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.400
But that's the thing.
It's, like, you're so amped up.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.167
You're like somebody, please,
like, I need, like,

00:03:06.167 --> 00:03:08.601
an exorcism of this anxiety.

00:03:08.601 --> 00:03:12.334
But at the same time, I'm, like,
too tired to be this excited.

00:03:12.334 --> 00:03:14.834
-It's the perfect --
-Right.

00:03:14.834 --> 00:03:17.033
-And I'll tell you this much --
when you're done,

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:19.000
you're going wish
that you did it one more time.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:20.200
-I agree.
-It's so fun.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:23.767
You go, "Man, that was
the most fun ride ever."

00:03:23.767 --> 00:03:24.834
-And congrats on everything.
-Yeah, I'm excited.

00:03:24.834 --> 00:03:26.734
-You deserve nothing
but the best.

00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:27.868
And I appreciate it.

00:03:27.868 --> 00:03:30.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:30.601 --> 00:03:32.767
-Yeah!

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:34.868 --> 00:03:36.334
Okay, first we got to get
a little lime.

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:38.133
-Yeah, alright.
-Ready?

00:03:38.133 --> 00:03:39.434
-I mean, Stephen A Smith --

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:41.133
My apologies to
Stephen A. Smith.

00:03:41.133 --> 00:03:42.133
-OK, wait, so this is what we
say.

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:43.300
This is what we say.

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:49.167
Pa arriba, pa abajo,
pa'l centro, pa'l dentro.

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:52.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.634 --> 00:03:55.133
Wow, he chugged it.

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:57.501
-I assumed that you had just
put apple juice or something

00:03:57.501 --> 00:03:59.434
in there, and nope.

00:03:59.434 --> 00:04:00.834
That is real deal.
-Congrats!

00:04:00.834 --> 00:04:01.834
You're drunk the rest
of the show.

00:04:01.834 --> 00:04:03.167
-Whoo!

00:04:03.167 --> 00:04:05.934
All right, party!

00:04:05.934 --> 00:04:10.033
Camila Cabello,
"Familia" is out right now.

00:04:10.033 --> 00:04:12.133
Check it out this weekend on
"Saturday Night Live."

